{"analysis":"The final error indicates an axis mismatch when computing `gamma_power`: `power` has shape (n_ev, 1, n_freq, n_time), so after indexing `power[:, 0, :, time_mask]` you get a 3D array (n_ev, n_freq, n_selected_times), not 4D. You should take the mean over axes (1,2) rather than (1,2,3). For example:

    gamma_power = power[:, 0, :, time_mask].mean(axis=(1,2))

Adjust the `mean` call accordingly and rerun.","success":false}

{"analysis":"The final error arises because after indexing `power[:, 0, :, time_mask]`, the resulting array has 3 dimensions (n_epochs, n_freq, n_time), so you must average over axes (1, 2), not (1, 2, 3). Update the aggregation line to:

    gamma_power = power[:, 0, :, time_mask].mean(axis=(1, 2))

Then rebuild the DataFrame and rerun the model.","success":false}
